A CSS declaration consists of two major parts: Selector and Declaration block.

General format:
Selector {
  property1: value1;
  property2: value2;
}

Rules:
- Selector = the HTML tag to apply styles to (e.g., p, h1, body)
- Declaration block = enclosed in curly braces { }
- Each property-value pair is separated by a colon (:)
- Each declaration ends with a semicolon (;)
- Multiple properties are separated by semicolons

Example:
p {
  font-size: 16pt;
  color: red;
  font-weight: bold;
}

A CSS rule consists of a Selector and a Declaration block:

Selector: The HTML tag (element) to which the style is applied. For example, 'p' selects all paragraph elements; 'h1' selects all level-1 headings.

Declaration Block: Enclosed in curly braces { }. Contains one or more property-value pairs, each ending with a semicolon. The property name and its value are separated by a colon.

Example:
p {
  font-size: 16pt;
  color: red;
  font-weight: bold;
}

This rule applies to all <p> tags: text will be 16pt, red, and bold. If this is an internal style, it goes inside <style>...</style> in the <head>. If external, it is saved as a .css file and linked with <link>.

CSS file content (save as heading_style.css):

h1 {
  font-family: "Comic Sans MS";
  font-style: italic;
  font-size: 24px;
  font-weight: bold;
  color: blue;
  border: 2px solid blue;
}

To link and use:

<html>
<head>
  <title> Heading Style Demo </title>
  <link rel='stylesheet' type='text/css' href='heading_style.css'>
</head>
<body>
  <h1> Welcome to CSS </h1>
</body>
</html>

Explanation: font-family sets the typeface; font-style: italic makes it italic; font-size sets the size in pixels; font-weight: bold makes it bold; the border adds a 2px solid blue border around the heading.

CSS Font and Text Properties:

1. color: Sets the colour of the text. Value: predefined colour name or hex code.
Example: p { color: pink; }

2. text-align: Sets horizontal alignment of text. Values: center, left, right, justify.
Example: p { text-align: center; }

3. font-family: Sets the typeface/font of the text. Value: font name (use quotes for multi-word names).
Example: p { font-family: 'Times New Roman'; }

4. font-style: Sets the style of the font. Values: normal, italic.
Example: p { font-style: italic; }

5. font-weight: Sets the weight (boldness) of the font. Values: normal, bold.
Example: p { font-weight: bold; }

6. font-size: Sets the size of the text in pixels.
Example: p { font-size: 14px; }

7. background-color: Sets the background colour of an element.
Example: body { background-color: violet; }

8. border: Sets a border around an element. Value: thickness style colour.
Example: h2 { border: 2px solid red; }

9. Margin properties (margin-top, margin-bottom, margin-left, margin-right): Set the margin space around an element in pixels.
Example: p { margin-top: 50px; margin-left: 50px; }
